  "details": "I have to admit they did an amazing job at revamping the games Ui but I can’t help but feel from playing back in 2019 to 2023 the UI feels and looks dull especially the nameplates I feel like they’re too much of the same now everyone has the same one and even though you can change the opacity it makes the game look clunky when they’re a lot of people in a room compared to the old one from 2019 where it was just a line of whatever colour trusted rank you were and the inside was completely clear which I feel like the colour added a better feeling to the game. And the quick menu isn’t actually a quick menu anymore you have to select worlds to get to the main settings now and it just feels off and hard to use sometimes whilst the old one showed everything you needed straight in front of you with easy access. I’m not saying to change the whole game I’m sure some people prefer the new UI but some people like myself loved the original one so maybe you could add an option to change the UI ( nameplates and menu’s) with a option that can be selected in settings so like . Say if it’s added the easiest way to access it would be to put it in a list like ;\n\n*2017 UI -/-\n\n*2018 UI -/-\n\n*2021 UI -/-\n\n*2023 UI -/-",
